    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "table-00002",
      "summary": "An illustration (table) shows the Names Structures and pKa of ammonium ion. Ammonia blue NH3 9.26. Primary alkylamine: Methylamine methyl group bonded to blue amino group 10.64; Ethylamine ethyl group bonded to blue amino group 10.75. Secondary alkylamine: Diethylamine two ethyl groups bonded to blue nitrogen monohydride 10.98. Pyrrolidine a cyclopentane with a blue nitrogen monohydride 11.27. Tertiary alkylamine: Triethylamine three ethyl groups bonded to blue nitrogen 10.76. Arylamine: Aniline benzene bonded to blue amino group 4.63. Heterocyclic amine: Pyridine benzene with a blue nitrogen 5.25; Pyrimidine benzene with two blue nitrogen atoms 1.3; Pyrrole a cyclopentane with two double bonds and a blue nitrogen monohydride 0.4; Imidazole a cyclopentane with a nitrogen monohydride and a blue nitrogen 6.95.",
